  "notes": "AUTHORITATIVE PAD MAP. Every one of the 900 pads is assigned explicitly from the get_900_matrix output, so nothing about the layout is inferred. This replaces a reconstruction that described the plate as 15 vertical strips cut into rectangular bands: that model tiled the grid and matched every printed label pad, and was still wrong. 40 of the 72 segments are staircases where they meet the rounded corners of the plate, and 60 of the 72 areas disagreed with this map -- segment 1 by more than a factor of two (15 pads assumed, 7 actual). Areas now range 1.355..8.470 cm2. ONE CELL BREAKS THE PLATE'S MIRROR SYMMETRY: row 2, column 44 is given to segment 33, where both the left-right and the top-bottom mirror put it in segment 67. Every other pad on the plate mirrors exactly. That makes 33 an 8-pad segment against 7 for its three symmetry partners (1, 4, 36), and 67 a 5-pad segment against 6 for its partners (37, 42, 72). It is transcribed here exactly as supplied and flagged rather than silently corrected; confirm it against get_900_matrix. SEGMENTS 33 AND 59 are not excluded. Earlier campaigns recorded them as 'open via / no response above noise' and they were dropped before evaluation, which meant every later run inherited that verdict without re-testing it, and a hole in a heat map reads to the eye as a cold spot. They are carried through like any other segment and judged on the data in front of them.",
